rmalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The degree type is used to add, alter, or subtract individual notes in the chord. The print-object attribute","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be used to keep the degree from printing separately when it has already taken into account in the text","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute of the kind element. The degree-value and degree-type text attributes specify how the value and type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the degree should be displayed.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree","title":"MXLDegree","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDegree"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDegree"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/Value-swift.struct":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Value-swift.struct","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Value"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The content of the degree-value type is a number indicating the degree of the chord (1 for the root, 3 for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"third, etc). The text attribute specifies how the value of the degree should be displayed. The symbol","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute indicates that a symbol should be used in specifying the degree. If the symbol attribute is present,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the value of the text attribute follows the symbol.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLDegree.Value","url":"\/documentation\/i